  "notes": "Priority-fix verification for NO_GO 156-002.\n\nROOT CAUSE OF ORIGINAL NO_GO: The first docker fix-worker (docker-156-002-fix) was OOM-killed before writing a .result — .tasks/task-156-002-fix.partial-result is the startup marker stub. The 156-002 source-of-truth result (.tasks/task-156-002.result, evaluationDecision=DONE, rubric correctness=95/test_coverage=90/scope_compliance=100/documentation=90) had already implemented every directive bullet. The fix-task was spawned because Brain saw the NO_GO status flip, not because the code was wrong.\n\nVERIFICATION PERFORMED (in-scope only — anchor rules 1+2 honored):\n1. src/core/config.ts:30-41 — `DeckentConfigWithPipeline = DeckentConfig & { dependency_pipeline_enabled?: boolean }` alias confirmed. JSDoc explains the field lives on ResolvedConfig (config-types.ts:490) but NOT on DeckentConfig — DeckentConfig (config-types.ts:69-312) was read end-to-end and has no `dependency_pipeline_enabled` member, validating the bridge.\n2. src/core/config.ts:522-654 — createDefaultConfig() returns `config: DeckentConfigWithPipeline` with `dependency_pipeline_enabled: true` at line 594 (JSDoc at 584-593 documents why true: eliminates DIRECTIVES race conditions; activates wave-based spawning + cascade-on-NO_GO + unblock-on-DONE).\n3. src/core/config.ts:876-877 — loadConfig() resolved-block pass-through: `(config as DeckentConfigWithPipeline).dependency_pipeline_enabled ?? true`.\n4. src/core/config.ts:1393-1394 — mergeConfigs() resolved-block pass-through: same `?? true` fallback.\n5. tests/core/config-defaults.test.ts — 3 regression tests confirmed:\n   - `dependency_pipeline_enabled is true by default` (the directive's explicit assertion)\n   - `createDefaultConfig() and getDefaultConfig() return the same default value`\n   - `returns a fresh object each call (no shared reference)` — singleton-return guard.\n\nVERIFY GATES:\n- `npx vitest run tests/core/config-defaults.test.ts` → 3/3 PASS (2ms, 236ms total).\n- `npx vite